+//    3a-r6 (user 2026-09-19, of that: "提早消失之后太不明显了，尤其是从 favorite
+//    区往 today 区域这种跨度比较大的距离的时候更不明显，几乎看不出来了 ... 直接做成
+//    到位之后，它才开始衰减。动效的时长不变，但是白卡的存在时间延后一些"): gone by
+//    110ms, the card was there for six frames of a long flight. What read as
+//    unclean in the first version was the fade *coinciding* with the landing;
+//    the two are now apart in time instead. The card is whole from the first
+//    frame that moves to the last, and sets down afterwards, where it landed:
+//    200ms on EASE_OUT (half gone in ~55ms -- a set-down, not a linger).
+//    ⚠ The 200ms and its curve are ours, measured off nothing. (If this does
+//    not read well either the user's fallback is no card at all.)
+inline constexpr base::TimeDelta kSidebarRowFlightDuration =
+    base::Milliseconds(300);
+inline constexpr gfx::Tween::Type kSidebarRowFlightTween =
+    gfx::Tween::FAST_OUT_SLOW_IN_3;
+inline constexpr double kSidebarRowFlightLiftInEnd = 0.08;
+inline constexpr base::TimeDelta kSidebarRowFlightSetDownDuration =
+    base::Milliseconds(200);
+inline constexpr gfx::Tween::Type kSidebarRowFlightSetDownTween =
+    gfx::Tween::EASE_OUT;
+
+// How strong the flying card's fill and shadow are at eased progress |t| of
+// the flight. The way down is the set-down's, after the flight.
+inline constexpr double SidebarRowFlightLift(double t) {
+  if (t <= 0.0) {
+    return 0.0;
+  }
+  return t < kSidebarRowFlightLiftInEnd ? t / kSidebarRowFlightLiftInEnd : 1.0;
+}
